{"summary":"Inspection of the checked-in source contradicts all three amendments: the tree already contains denitrification logic driven by NO3, DOC, suboxic pore volume, and denitrifier activity; it defines denitrification parameters and defaults; and it tracks N2 export explicitly in the nitrogen budget with dedicated denitrification tests.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-325f0882","decision":"reject","rationale":"`crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs` already includes a denitrification phase after nitrification. It computes `suboxic_pore_volume_l` from `state.substrate_suboxic_pore_volume_cm3()`, applies Monod terms for pore-water NO3 and DOC, scales by `state.microbe.denitrifier_activity_index`, removes nitrate, increments `state.cumulative_n2_export_mg_n`, and returns alkalinity via `DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N`. `crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs` also defines explicit oxic/suboxic zone geometry and pore-volume helpers; the denitrifier state lives in `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs`, which is an appropriate location. The amendment’s factual premise is therefore incorrect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-a56c3028","decision":"reject","rationale":"The denitrification parameter surface is present in `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs`: `denitrification_vmax_mg_n_per_l_per_hour`, `denitrification_k_no3_mg_n_per_l`, `denitrification_k_doc_mg_c_per_l`, `denitrification_pore_water_mixing_factor`, and `denitrification_activity_maturation_days`. Those fields are populated in `ProcessParams::default()` and backed by explicit default helper functions. `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml` also contains corresponding denitrification defaults. This amendment does not match the current implementation."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-4cbac42a","decision":"reject","rationale":"Explicit N2 export accounting is already wired into the nitrogen budget through `cumulative_n2_export_mg_n`. `crates/tank_core/src/types/budget.rs` includes that field in `nitrogen_budget_components`, and `total_nitrogen_mg` sums those components, so denitrification is represented as transfer into a tracked export pool rather than an unexplained leak. The unchanged open-system action exemption in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` is not a problem because no special exemption is needed once the export pool is part of the closed-system ledger. The tree also has dedicated denitrification coverage in `crates/tank_core/tests/denitrification.rs`, including checks for export tracking and zero net nitrogen imbalance for the nitrogen-cycle stage."}]}